WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:34.630
Roxy arrived at the construction site in the mountains.

2
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.633
Detective Smith stood in front of the big, bronze door.

3
00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:38.153
It was still closed.

4
00:00:39.214 --> 00:00:39.854
"Hey, Detective!"

5
00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:40.135
Roxy said.

6
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:41.736
"Did you ring the doorbell to see if anyone's—?"

7
00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:43.277
"Shh!" Detective Smith put a finger to his lips.

8
00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:44.018
He looked scared.

9
00:00:44.038 --> 00:00:44.658
Roxy held up her hands.

10
00:00:44.678 --> 00:00:46.380
"Okay, okay," she whispered.

11
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.421
"Did you try opening the door?"

12
00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:48.261
The detective shook his head.

13
00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.842
"I don't know what's in there.

14
00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:51.424
But it's quiet now, and I want to keep it that way."

15
00:00:51.444 --> 00:00:52.925
"Well, we probably need to know what's in there."

16
00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:53.846
Roxy pushed on the door, but it didn't budge.

17
00:00:53.866 --> 00:00:55.127
"Grr!" Roxy pushed again.

18
00:00:55.547 --> 00:00:56.888
The door still wouldn't open.

19
00:00:56.908 --> 00:00:59.170
"Hmph!" Roxy said.

20
00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.352
"Stand back, Detective."

21
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:05.117
Whiz-hoo! Roxy fired her eye laser beams.

22
00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:07.778
They bounced off the door and shot right back at her.

23
00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:12.119
"Yikes!" Roxy ducked, and the beams hit a huge boulder.

24
00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:13.599
The boulder exploded.

25
00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.080
"Whoa!" Detective Smith said.

26
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.201
"That door is strong!"

27
00:01:18.621 --> 00:01:19.701
Roxy stared at the door.

28
00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:22.502
Orange beams radiated from her eyes.

29
00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.982
She expected the door to heat up and melt.

30
00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:26.823
But that didn't happen.

31
00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:29.964
Next she used her freeze breath.

32
00:01:32.172 --> 00:01:33.773
That had no effect on the door either.

33
00:01:34.814 --> 00:01:37.515
"I can't believe this."

34
00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:38.816
Roxy moaned.

35
00:01:38.836 --> 00:01:41.277
"I'm the most powerful person on Earth.

36
00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:43.579
And I can't even open a door!"

37
00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:46.560
"What about your x-ray vision?"

38
00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:48.041
Detective Smith said.

39
00:01:48.061 --> 00:01:50.983
"Maybe you can at least see what's on the other side."

40
00:01:51.003 --> 00:01:52.344
"Good idea."

41
00:01:53.204 --> 00:01:54.605
Roxy stared at the door again.

42
00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:02.102
a tunnel that goes down, but it's really long and really dark.

43
00:02:02.682 --> 00:02:03.863
I can't see where it goes."

44
00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:05.544
She sighed.

45
00:02:05.564 --> 00:02:08.567
"It's no use, Detective.

46
00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:11.649
I can't open the door or see what made the noise."

47
00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.291
She tapped her chin.

48
00:02:13.311 --> 00:02:16.653
"But I know someone who can—maybe."

49
00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:22.478
Cozlin," Febby said.

50
00:02:22.498 --> 00:02:25.380
"What would you buy if you had a million partecs?"

51
00:02:26.081 --> 00:02:27.962
Cozlin and her friends were out at recess.

52
00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:29.584
They were playing zip disk.

53
00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:30.909
"I don't know."

54
00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:32.850
Cozlin ran with the disk.

55
00:02:33.411 --> 00:02:36.193
"I guess a new suspension pool would be fun."

56
00:02:36.914 --> 00:02:38.575
She took a shot at the goal and missed.

57
00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:40.597
Mert got the disk.

58
00:02:41.137 --> 00:02:44.940
"You don't need a million partecs to buy a suspension pool."

59
00:02:45.821 --> 00:02:48.163
He tried to take a shot, but Drupp stole the disk.

60
00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:51.846
"What would you buy with a million partecs, Drupp?"

61
00:02:52.266 --> 00:02:53.067
Cozlin asked.

62
00:02:53.827 --> 00:02:55.128
Drupp ran across the court.

63
00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:57.530
"I'd buy a space ski."

64
00:02:58.391 --> 00:02:59.472
Mert rolled his eyes.

65
00:02:59.936 --> 00:03:03.898
"You don't need a million partecs for a space ski either."

66
00:03:03.918 --> 00:03:07.279
Drupp sent the disk zipping into the goal.

67
00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:12.642
"You do if it's a hyperspace ski!"

68
00:03:13.742 --> 00:03:14.503
Everyone laughed.

69
00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:18.885
Cozlin's watch beeped.

70
00:03:18.905 --> 00:03:20.766
"I'll be right back.

71
00:03:21.346 --> 00:03:22.606
I'm thirsty!"

72
00:03:24.147 --> 00:03:25.828
She stepped away and opened her watch.

73
00:03:29.932 --> 00:03:30.753
"Hey, Roxy!"

74
00:03:31.153 --> 00:03:32.054
Cozlin smiled.

75
00:03:32.074 --> 00:03:33.194
"What's up?"

76
00:03:34.035 --> 00:03:34.856
Roxy frowned.

77
00:03:34.876 --> 00:03:36.857
"I've got a big problem."

78
00:03:36.877 --> 00:03:40.840
"Is a big monster destroying Metro City?"

79
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.001
Cozlin asked.

80
00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.002
"Are robots invading Earth?"

81
00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:45.824
Roxy shook her head.

82
00:03:45.844 --> 00:03:49.486
"Don't laugh, but there's a door I can't open."

83
00:03:50.327 --> 00:03:51.528
Cozlin scratched her head.

84
00:03:51.548 --> 00:03:54.530
"That doesn't sound like a big problem, Roxy."

85
00:03:55.431 --> 00:03:57.052
"I know," Roxy said.

86
00:03:57.548 --> 00:03:59.912
"But something big is behind the door.

87
00:04:00.393 --> 00:04:01.655
We need to know what it is.

88
00:04:02.176 --> 00:04:06.342
And since you can walk through walls Cozlin grinned.

89
00:04:06.362 --> 00:04:07.965
"Don't worry, Roxy.

90
00:04:08.425 --> 00:04:09.527
I'm on my way!"
